{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Computation and Computer Architecture"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about computation and computer architecture."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify key information about people's jobs and places of work in spoken or written contexts. Make the information system design report, based on the selection of both hardware and software tools required for the IT solution."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understand important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.  Exchange simple information on the design of an information system, computer architecture and hardware, and basic concepts on graphic design."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Quantifiers: Too Many and Too Much"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <strong>quantifiers</strong> to express the quantity of something. In this order, quantifiers modify nouns in terms of amount."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>Two common <strong>quantifiers</strong> are: <strong><i>Too many</i></strong> and <strong><i>too much</i></strong></p> <p>You use <strong><i>too many</i></strong> with countable nouns in plural.&nbsp;</p> <p>Example:</p> <p><i>There are <strong>too many </strong></i>programs for each specific task in the computer.</p> <p>You use <strong><i>too much</i></strong> with uncountable nouns in singular (due to their condition of uncountable nouns there&rsquo;s no plural form for them).&nbsp;</p> <p>Example:</p> <p><i>He has <strong>too much </strong>experience in computer architecture.</i></p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "He predicted too many features that modern computers have today, such as the data stored in the internal memory of machines."}, {"type": "example", "content": "As you can see, there were too many prototypes of computers until the most recent versions nowadays."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Steve Jobs developed too many important ideas about it."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":1,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Too Many</br><div class=\\\"center_text\\\">(Countable nouns)\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Singular\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Plural\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>- Program</br> - Computer</br> - Field</br> - Design\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>- Programs</br> - Computers</br> - Fields</br> - Designs</br>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Too Much</br><div class=\\\"center_text\\\">(Uncountable nouns)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div align=\\\"center\\\"><strong>Singular\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<i>- Experience</br> - Performance</br> - Information</br> - Time\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Steve Jobs"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<strong>Steve Jobs</strong> is one of the most important genius in the computing technology. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "He was the inventor of the first personal computer and the founder of Apple Computer Company. He was a visionary that worked very hard to take advantage of technology transforming it into entertainment for users around the world. </br></br> Check this brief profile about his life: "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":14,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Steve Jobs</span></div></br> <div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\"> (1955-2011) </span></div>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":13,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">1955</span></div></br>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Steven Paul Jobs was born in San Francisco, United States. He was adopted by Paul and Clara Jobs.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">1972</span></div></br>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He got into The Reed College University in Portland   (Oregon). He studied only for six months due to the high costs of his studies.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">1976</span></div></br>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He founded Apple Computer Company. In ten years, this company got 4000 employees. The first computer was the Apple I, considered as the first personal computer.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">1983</span></div></br>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Apple released Lisa (GUI), another personal computer that offered a graphical user interface. This project was unsuccessful due to the high cost of this computer in that time.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">1984</span></div></br>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Jobs and his friend Steve Wozniak released the Macintosh computer. It was the first computer with mouse.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">1985</span></div></br>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Jobs left Apple due to some disagreements with John Sculley, the executive director of his own company. Sculley was in other times the executive director of Pepsi-Cola and Jobs persuaded him to work for Apple, with the intention to keep the competitiveness of his company.This year he founded NeXT Computer.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">1986</span></div></br>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Jobs bought the enterprise The Graphics group, which will become Pixar later.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">1996</span></div></br>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Apple bought NeXT Computer, which meant the return of Jobs to the company.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">1998</span></div></br>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Apple released the iMac, a computer designed to surf on the Internet.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">2001</span></div></br>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Jobs released the iPod, a portable media player.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">2007</span></div></br>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Jobs released the iPhone, a smart phone that revolutionized the concept of entertainment in mobile technology.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">2011</span></div></br>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Jobs died due to a pancreatic cancer that was diagnosed in 2003.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Steve Jobs developed too many important ideas about it. He founded Apple Computer Company in 1976."}, {"type": "example", "content": "He released the first computer with mouse, the Macintosh."}, {"type": "example", "content": "In 1998, Apple launched the iMac, a computer with access to Internet."}, {"type": "image", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob11img01.jpg"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "internal"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "located in the inner part of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He predicted too many features that modern computers have today, such as the data stored in the internal memory of machines."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob11aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "RAM memory "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "(Random Access Memory) it is a device used to store data which let read or write these ones in a faster way "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He predicted too many features that modern computers have today, such as the data stored in the internal memory of machines, the use of a RAM memory or fast memory to hold commands."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob11aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "aerodynamics"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the analysis of air or other gases motion"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He started to work on aerodynamics and ballistics problems."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob11aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "programmable calculator "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "device that allows you to make calculations, the first computers were programmable calculators"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: As these problems required machine assistance, he had the opportunity to know the programmable calculator \u201cHarvard Mark I\u201d."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob11aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "prototype"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a model, a design"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: As you can see, there were too many prototypes of computers until the most recent versions nowadays."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob11aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "magnetism"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something with the property of attraction due to a magnet"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Neumann devise a design that could have some marks that indicated the memory by voltage or magnetism."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le01ob11aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Do some research about computer architecture. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a dialogue where you explain the importance of the computer architecture. "}, {"