 some questions about computation. What happened with the ENIAC?<br/>\n<strong>Linda:</strong> Neumann took some ideas from the ENIAC to devise a design that could store information in a functional way with the binary system, likewise some marks that indicated the memory by voltage or magnetism.<br/>\n<strong>Thomas:</strong> Who else made important contributions to computation?<br/>\n<strong>Linda: </strong>Steve Jobs developed too many important ideas about it. He founded Apple Computer Company in 1976, which launched Lisa (GUI) a computer with a graphical user interface. Years later, he released the first computer with a mouse, the Macintosh. In 1998, Apple launched the iMac, a computer with access to the Internet."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n4le01ob11re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "type": "scholar"}]}